  <!-- EDUCATIONAL SEO ARTICLE CONTENT -->
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <div class="space-y-8 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">What is a PPF Calculator?</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          A <strong>Public Provident Fund (PPF) Calculator</strong> is a specialized financial planning tool designed to estimate how your savings compound over a 15-year statutory lock-in period and subsequent 5-year extension tranches. By specifying your contribution frequency (yearly or monthly), deposit amount, deposit timing, and the prevailing or assumed annual interest rate, the calculator accurately generates the total principal invested, accumulated interest, and the final tax-free maturity corpus.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">What is Public Provident Fund (PPF)?</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The <strong>Public Provident Fund (PPF)</strong> is a government-backed long-term savings and retirement scheme introduced in India by the National Savings Institute under the Ministry of Finance. It offers a sovereign guarantee on capital safety and interest payments.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-xs">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-3.5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">⭐ EEE Tax Benefit</div>
            <p class="mt-1 text-slate-500">Exempt at investment (Section 80C up to ₹1.5L/yr), Exempt on interest accrual, and Exempt on maturity.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-3.5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">🔒 Sovereign Guarantee</div>
            <p class="mt-1 text-slate-500">Backed directly by the Government of India, making it completely immune to market volatility and credit risks.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-3.5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">🛡️ Court Attachment Immunity</div>
            <p class="mt-1 text-slate-500">Under the PPF Act, the account balance cannot be attached by any court decree or creditor claims.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">How Does a PPF Calculator Work?</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The calculation follows a strict annual recursive model based on official Indian Post Office and banking rules:
        </p>
        <div class="mt-3 rounded-2xl bg-slate-100 p-4 font-mono text-xs dark:bg-slate-800/80 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
          Opening Balance + Current Year Deposit + Annual Interest - Withdrawals = Closing Balance
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          For each financial year, the closing balance of the previous year serves as the opening balance of the next year. Because interest is compounded annually and added to the principal, the interest earned in subsequent years grows exponentially.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">PPF Interest Calculation Formula and Timing Nuance</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The Ministry of Finance sets PPF interest rates quarterly. By law, interest is calculated <strong>monthly</strong> on the <strong>lowest balance between the close of the 5th day and the last day of each calendar month</strong>, and then credited annually on March 31.
        </p>

        <div class="my-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
            The Golden Rule: Deposit On or Before the 5th of the Month
          </h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            <li>
              <strong>Lump Sum Investors:</strong> Depositing on or before <strong>April 5</strong> ensures your deposit earns interest for the entire 12 months of the financial year. Depositing after April 5 means that installment forfeits interest for April.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Monthly SIP Investors:</strong> Depositing on or before the <strong>5th of every month</strong> ensures that installment earns interest for that calendar month. Depositing after the 5th earns interest only starting from the subsequent month.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
          For equal annual deposits at the beginning of each year, the future value <var>F</var> can be represented by the annuity future value equation:
        </p>
        <div class="my-2 rounded-2xl bg-slate-100 p-3 font-mono text-xs text-center dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          F = P &times; [((1 + <var>i</var>)<sup><var>n</var></sup> - 1) / <var>i</var>] &times; (1 + <var>i</var>)
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-2 text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-2">
          <div><strong>F:</strong> Maturity Value</div>
          <div><strong>P:</strong> Periodic Deposit</div>
          <div><strong>i:</strong> Annual Interest Rate (<var>r</var> / 100)</div>
          <div><strong>n:</strong> Number of Years (15 to 30)</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Comprehensive PPF Calculation Examples</h2>

        <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs">
          <!-- Example 1 -->
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4.5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-2">
            <span class="font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 uppercase tracking-wider text-[11px]">Example 1: Moderate Saver</span>
